course: dictionary
lesson: 14057
title: A word from the kitchen
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: You may meet a word you have never seen before, like masher. Read the words around it, because they are its context and they leave clues. «Mum used a masher to crush the boiled potatoes until they were soft.» The clues are crush, boiled potatoes and soft. So a masher is something you use on food.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence: «Mum used a kitchen tool to crush the boiled potatoes until they were soft.» It still makes sense, so your meaning fits.
explain: Masher also has an old-fashioned meaning: a man who made unwanted advances to women in public. This sense is old and rarely used now. The kitchen tool is the meaning you will meet most.
fact: A masher is a kitchen tool with a handle and a flat head with holes or a wavy wire.
fact: You use a «potato masher» to crush cooked potatoes into a soft mush.
fact: Cooks also use a masher for swede, banana and other soft food, such as baby food.
fact: In history, a German WWII grenade was nicknamed «potato masher» because of its shape.
fact: The old slang meaning, a man who made unwanted advances to women in public, is rarely used now.
exercise: «Mum pressed the masher down into the boiled potatoes until they were soft.» What is a masher? | A tall hat worn by Victorian gentlemen | A small wooden spoon for stirring tea | *A kitchen tool for crushing soft food | A bowl for washing lettuce
exercise: «Dad used the masher to make the swede smooth for baby Sam.» What is the masher's job? | *To crush the food into a soft mush | To keep the food cold | To grind coffee beans | To cut bread into thin slices
exercise: «Dad used the masher, then added butter and milk to the potatoes.» What kind of thing is a masher most likely to be? | A type of horse | A song | *A kitchen tool | A kind of bread
test: What is a potato masher used for? | Cutting raw carrots into thin rings | *Crushing cooked potatoes into a soft mush | Boiling water quickly | Keeping ice cream frozen
test: In history, what was the German WWII grenade nicknamed because of its shape? | Pineapple | Egg | *Potato masher | Cricket ball
exam: Which word is the kitchen tool in «Mum needs a masher for the potatoes»? | for | needs | *masher | potatoes
